  "contract": "Previously rejected literal patterns compare at the actual C expression width without narrowing into the subject. One saved subject and lazy pattern order remain. The decimal -9223372036854775808LL comparison uses a generated C adapter compiled by the actual selected CC, whose extended signed versus unsigned interpretation differs. Ordinary values stay in Rust. The adapter travels with independently built RS libraries and sealed artifacts; helper allocation reserves Rust and private C symbols. Bare --emit-rust continues to reject programs requiring native C support.",
  "independent_controls": "Foreign native integer inputs execute positive and negative branches across narrow/wide signed and unsigned subjects, C widths, counters/laziness, native C-only helper-name collisions; two independently namespaced RS implementations and one C reference are consumed by C/Rust through source and sealed artifacts.",
